    "note": "Source: Grameen One: Scheme Two 'Equity Investments at Market' statement, statement date 31-Dec-15 (AIMS of Bangladesh Limited, Asset Manager). Excludes: BRAC Bank Convertible Bonds and IBBLPBond (bonds, listed under the EQUITY heading in the source but not equity/MF units), 4 Pre-IPO holdings, and 1 Not Listed holding -- none are listed equity/MF holdings. Source PDF provides only Acquisition Cost and Market Value per holding (no share/unit count column). Share counts were derived by dividing each holding's market value by its DSE closing price on 2015-12-31 from this app's own historical_prices data (which reproduced clean round-lot share counts for ~94 of 103 holdings, confirming the method). For 9 holdings lacking usable 2015-12-31 price data, shares were derived either by continuity with an adjacent GRAMEENS2 quarter file showing an identical cost basis (MICEMENT, BSCPLC, SALVO, RNSPIN -- unchanged position => same share count), a par-value (Tk 10/unit) inference (RUPALILIFEMF), or a labeled best-effort round-number estimate where no price or continuity data exists at all (SANDHANILG, SPPCL, 1STICB, 2NDICB -- these 4 total just ~0.09M BDT of cost, under 0.01% of the portfolio). Cost/Market values for ALL holdings (including these 9) are taken directly from the PDF and are exact, not estimated. Checksum: sum of all 110 PDF line items (103 equity/MF + 2 bonds + 4 pre-IPO + 1 not-listed) = cost 1,067,780,590.71 / mkt 1,956,535,605, matching the PDF's printed TOTAL MARKET VALUE row (1,067,780,591 / 1,956,535,604) to within rounding."
